1 21-12-105. Career and technical education
2 demonstration project grants; application; criteria;
3 limitations.
4
5 (b) Any amount awarded to a district under this
6 section shall be in addition to and not be considered in
7 determining the school foundation program amount under the
8 education resource block grant model pursuant to W.S.
9 21-13-309 and the amount for career and technical education
10 supplies, materials and equipment pursuant to W.S.
11 21-13-338. A grant awarded under this section shall be for
12 a period of two (2) years and shall not exceed one hundred
13 fifty thousand dollars ($150,000.00) for the first year of
14 demonstration project planning, and not more than two
15 hundred thousand dollars ($200,000.00) for project
16 implementation in year two (2) of the project
17 grant. Thereafter, state assistance for the project shall
18 be limited to funds distributed to the district within its
19 foundation program amount as determined under the education
20 resource block grant model and the amount distributed under
21 W.S. 21-13-338. Any school district receiving funds under
22 W.S. 21-13-337 for career and technical supplies, materials
23 and equipment shall be ineligible to receive a grant under
5 HB0235

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0685
1 this section for the period the district receives funds
2 under W.S. 21-13-337.
