4 21-13-337. Career and technical education equipment
5 grants; application; criteria; limitations.
6
7 (a) A school district may apply to the state
8 department of education for state assistance to fund the
9 purchase of supplies, materials and equipment for a new or
10 existing career and technical education program in the
11 district. Amounts awarded under this section shall be in
12 addition to and shall not be considered in determining the
13 school foundation program amount under the education
14 resource block grant model pursuant to W.S. 21-13-309 and
15 shall be in addition to the amount for career and technical
16 education supplies, materials and equipment pursuant to
17 W.S. 21-13-338. Any school district receiving funds under
18 W.S. 21-12-105 for a career and technical education
19 demonstration project grant shall be ineligible to receive
20 funds under this section for the period the district
21 receives funds under W.S. 21-12-105.
22
7 HB0235

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0685
1 (c) Not later than August 15 of the applicable school
2 year and following review of applications submitted under
3 this section, the department shall notify applicant
4 districts of its grant awards and shall provide each
5 applicant district a written statement of the reasons for
6 approving or denying the application. No award shall be
7 given to a district unless it has expended, or will expend
8 with the award of the grant requested under this section,
9 the entire amount generated under W.S. 21-13-309(m)(v)(D)
10 prior to school year 2025-2026 for supplies, materials and
11 equipment for career and technical education programs and
12 commencing school year 2025-2026, the entire amount
13 generated under W.S. 21-13-338 for supplies, materials and
14 equipment for career and technical education programs
15 utilizing expenditure data from the immediately preceding
16 five (5) school years from the date of application and
17 amounts from the special reserve fund created under W.S.
18 21-13-504 for supplies, materials and equipment for career
19 and technical education programs. Further Preference shall
20 be given to districts that have not received a grant under
21 this section in the immediately preceding five (5) school
22 years from the date of application. If an application is
23 approved, the department shall award the grant from amounts
